@@section 1
@@title CQ-SINK Visual sinking: no bump between sunken blocks, even depth, items on top, 2026-11-10 ([blockrunner.md](../blockrunner.md) 3.4, TODO `gameplay/blockrunner #7`)
@@date 2026-11-10
@@jars creativecompat creativedevtools
@@sources feature_writeup/blockrunner.md
@@text
@@text Needs the 2026-11-10 Creative Compat jar in `mods/`. Client only (rendering); default `[surface.sinking] depthPixels = 2`, raise to 8 to see it easily.
@@text
@@table
## CQ-SINK-01
@group client
@commands BR-53 and BR-55: first person, walk slowly slime -> honey -> slime, wool -> mud -> wool, wool -> dirt path; walk to a wool edge over a 1-block drop
@pass LOOK: no upward pop at any seam; at the edge the view stays sunk until you fall
@fails `SinkingRender.depthAt` corner fallback; `support` top check
@owner true
@draft walking feel across seams and a ledge (BR-53, BR-55): a person judges the view in motion; a `walk` step plus shots could stage it, but the pass is a feel
## CQ-SINK-02
@group client
@commands BR-54: F5, a pig on wool beside a pig on a honey block
@pass LOOK: equal depth
@fails `support` own-sink branch
@reviewed 2026-11-16
# side by side in front of the player (yaw 0 faces +z; at yaw 90 both pigs were out of view, one behind the other)
> fill ~-3 ~-1 ~4 ~-1 ~-1 ~4 minecraft:white_wool
> fill ~1 ~-1 ~4 ~3 ~-1 ~4 minecraft:honey_block
> summon minecraft:pig ~-2 ~ ~4 {NoAI:1b}
> summon minecraft:pig ~2 ~ ~4 {NoAI:1b}
do {"look": {"yaw": 0, "pitch": 10}}
do {"wait": 20}
shot pigs_side
look the two pigs sink to equal depth (the F5 third-person view of the row is the same judgement on any pig)
## CQ-SINK-03
@group client
@commands BR-56: drop items on wool, sand, slime; then add sand to `creativecompat:sinking_hides_items` in `blocktags.js`, `/reload`
@pass LOOK: items lie on the texture; after the edit the sand item sinks in, wool unchanged; revert the edit
@fails `HIDES_ITEMS` check in `support`; ItemPhysic renders through `EntityRenderDispatcher#render`
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> setblock ~ ~-1 ~3 minecraft:white_wool
> setblock ~2 ~-1 ~3 minecraft:sand
> setblock ~-2 ~-1 ~3 minecraft:slime_block
> summon minecraft:item ~ ~1 ~3 {Item:{id:"minecraft:apple",Count:1b}}
> summon minecraft:item ~2 ~1 ~3 {Item:{id:"minecraft:apple",Count:1b}}
> summon minecraft:item ~-2 ~1 ~3 {Item:{id:"minecraft:apple",Count:1b}}
do {"look": {"yaw": 0, "pitch": 35}}
do {"wait": 40}
shot items_on_blocks
look items lie on the texture of wool, sand and slime. The tag-edit half (add sand to `creativecompat:sinking_hides_items` in blocktags.js, /reload, the sand item sinks in, revert) edits a pack script: do it by hand in the same session

@@section 2
@@title CQ-SINK Layer blocks stand, sink and slow the same at every layer count, 2026-11-18 ([blockrunner.md](../blockrunner.md) 3.11, TODO `gameplay/blockrunner #13`)
@@date 2026-11-18
@@jars creativecompat creativedelight
@@sources feature_writeup/blockrunner.md
@@text
@@text Needs the 2026-11-18 Creative Compat and Creative Delight jars in `mods/` and `blocktags.js` as of 2026-11-18. Full restart (mixins, Java). Default `[surface.sinking] depthPixels = 2`.
@@text
@@table
## CQ-SINK-04
@group client
@commands BR-89: on stone, rows of 1, 2, 4 and 7 layers of IW sand, IW ash, Supplementaries ash, salt, IE sawdust and fodder; stand on each, `/data get entity @s Pos`; then 2 layers of IW ash on a full ash layer stack
@pass feet 2 px per layer above the stone for every block at the same count (sawdust 2n-1 px); IW ash over ash holds you
@fails `IwLayerCollisionMixin`, `SuppAshCollisionMixin`, `IeSawdustCollisionMixin` not applied (CompatMixinPlugin gate, mod id); salt: Vintage Delight `SaltLayerBlock.getCollisionShape`
@owner true
@draft standing heights per block and count: a `tp` + `data get` loop could read them, the rows are hand-built
## CQ-SINK-05
@group client
@commands BR-90: first person, walk slowly across the rows of CQ-SINK-04 and from a 7-layer sand onto a sand block; drop an item on each
@pass LOOK: the same sink at every block and count, no pop at the seams; items lie on top
@fails `SinkingRender.support` surface layer branch; `#creativecompat:surface_layers` or `#creativecompat:sinking` missing the block
@owner true
@draft view feel in motion; a person judges it
## CQ-SINK-06
@group client
@commands BR-91: WTHIT on 1 layer of salt, sand, ash, sawdust, fodder on stone; a 1-layer leaf pile and 1 snow layer; walk a 20-block strip of 1-layer sand and one of sand blocks
@pass "0.85× (Dust)" on salt, sand, ash, sawdust; "0.88× (Soft)" on fodder; leaf pile and snow unchanged; both strips take the same time
@fails `SurfaceLayers.afterBlockRunner` (BlockRunnerBlockStateMixin), `RunSpeed.at` standable rule; salt not in `blockrunner:surface/dust`
@owner true
@draft WTHIT lines and walking time; WTHIT needs the client, the strip timing could be a bot walk
## CQ-SINK-07
@group client
@commands BR-92: survival; fall 10 blocks onto 4 and 8 layers of sand, IW ash, Supplementaries ash, salt and onto stone (`/tp` above each, note health)
@pass the same damage on every pile and on stone
@fails `IwLayerRulesMixin` / `IwSandLayerFallMixin` / `SuppAshRulesMixin` redirect not applied (`require = 0`: check the mixin log); `SurfaceLayers.fallDamage`
@owner true
@draft health deltas per pile; a bot fall plus `data get entity @s Health` could read them
## CQ-SINK-08
@group client
@commands BR-93: sand layer item on 8 sand layers; red sand the same; salt dust on 8 salt layers; dispenser with salt into 8 salt; break the support under 3 sand layers above 8 sand layers, and 3 salt over 8 salt; craft 1 sand and 9 sand layers
@pass a full block each time, the rest (2 layers) on top for the falling cases; 1 sand -> 9 layers, 9 layers -> 1 sand
@fails `SurfaceLayers.settle` (IW `onPlace` hook), Vintage Delight `SaltLayerBlock.settle` / `SaltDustItem`, Salt member `Melting.placeSaltLayer`; recipes: Creative Compat `misc_mods.js`
@owner true
@draft block results per case; `setblock` + `data get block`-style checks could automate most of it
## CQ-SINK-09
@group client
@commands BR-94: place cobblestone against 1 layer of sand, IW ash, Supplementaries ash, salt, sawdust, fodder; against 1 and 3 layers of snow, a leaf pile, bamboo leaves; then 4 layers; break 5 layers of fodder and of sand
@pass surface layers stay (block on top); walk-through layers of 1 and 3 replaced, 4 not; sand drops 5 layers; note what fodder drops
@fails `SurfaceLayers.replaceable`, `#creativecompat:replaceable_layers`; salt `SaltLayerBlock.canBeReplaced`
@owner true
@draft placement outcomes; a person places blocks
